<section | Self-closing DSL-registry tag>

A self-closing `<table />` should parse as a self-closing tag, not as a
long-form opener missing its closer. Before the alpha Phase 2 fix the DSL-
registry's long-form finder would greedily claim `<table />` and treat the
missing `</table>` as a tag error.

<table />

Surrounding prose continues to render normally after the self-closing tag.

<section | Visible parse-error rendering>

A deliberate parse error: an unknown escape sequence in named-tag content
produces an `enscribeParseError` node. The always-renders guarantee
requires it to render visibly at its source location, not fall through
silently.

<aside | This aside has an unknown escape: \z and then more prose.>

Surrounding content continues to render normally — the error is bounded to
its construct.
